\begin{abstract}
We study the open string spectrum of a class of toric Calabi-Yau threefolds, which are crepant resolutions of the orbifold $\mathbb{C}^3/\mathbb{Z}_3$. We show that the open string spectrum is described by a quiver gauge theory with gauge group $U(1)^3$ and $N_f=3$ fundamental hypermultiplets. We also show that the open string spectrum is invariant under the action of the modular group $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$.
\end{abstract}

\end{document}

\section{Introduction}

The study of open string spectra of Calabi-Yau threefolds has been an active area of research in recent years. The open string spectrum of a Calabi-Yau threefold $X$ is described by a quiver gauge theory with gauge group $U(1)^3$ and $N_f=3$ fundamental hypermultiplets. The quiver gauge theory is determined by the toric data of $X$. The open string spectrum is invariant under the action of the modular group $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$.

In this paper, we study the open string spectrum of a class of toric Calabi-Yau threefolds, which are crepant resolutions of the orbifold $\mathbb{C}^3/\mathbb{Z}_3$. We show that the open string spectrum is described by a quiver gauge theory with gauge group $U(1)^3$ and $N_f=3$ fundamental hypermultiplets. We also show that the open string spectrum is invariant under the action of the modular group $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$.

The paper is organized as follows. In section 2, we review the construction of the crepant resolution of the orbifold $\mathbb{C}^3/\mathbb{Z}_3$. In section 3, we study the open string spectrum of the crepant resolution. In section 4, we show that the open string spectrum is invariant under the action of the modular group $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$.

