\begin{quote}
\textbf{Abstract:}
\textit{
Liver cancer is the fifth most common cancer in the world. The early detection of liver cancer is crucial for the treatment of liver cancer. The automatic segmentation of liver and tumor in CT scans is an important step in the early detection of liver cancer. However, the liver and tumor in CT scans are often small and have similar intensity values, which makes the segmentation of liver and tumor in CT scans challenging. In this paper, we propose a hybrid deep attention-aware network (RA-UNet) to extract liver and tumor in CT scans. The RA-UNet consists of a Residual Attention (RA) module and a U-Net. The RA module is used to extract the features of liver and tumor in CT scans. The U-Net is used to fuse the features extracted by the RA module and generate the segmentation results. The RA module is designed to extract the features of liver and tumor in CT scans by using the attention mechanism. The attention mechanism can focus on the important features of liver and tumor in CT scans and ignore the unimportant features. The experimental results show that the proposed RA-UNet can extract liver and tumor in CT scans with high accuracy. The proposed RA-UNet can be used for the early detection of liver cancer.
}
\end{quote}

